In attempting to learn to use the lance, I've discovered a
rather major downside to it (other than its great weight):
applying it causes it to be wielded (like a pick-axe), and
it cannot be applied to anything adjacent to you.

This means that when a monster closes to melee
range, you are reduced to three options:
1. Try to get out of melee range.  This can be a little
   difficult when the monster is very nearly as fast as
   you, very difficult if it's faster than you.
2. Spend a turn switching weapons.
3. Begin bashing monsters with your lance.

In other words, it has the major shortcomings of
a bow or sling, without most of their range.

It's also impossible to use in diagonal corridors.

Plus it misses more often than a longsword.

Maybe it's a lot better when you're mounted?
Because as it stands right now, I'm sorely tempted
to re-adopt the policy of dropping the lance on
dungeon level one.


